
This directory is intended for PlatformIO Test Runner and project tests.

Unit Testing is a software testing method by which individual units of
source code, sets of one or more MCU program modules together with associated
control data, usage procedures, and operating procedures, are tested to
determine whether they are fit for use. Unit testing finds problems early
in the development cycle.

More information about PlatformIO Unit Testing:
- https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html

## ESP8266 LittleFS physical-reboot queue integration test

This opt-in test uses real LittleFS and physical ESP8266 resets; it does not
connect to Wi-Fi/MQTT, call `LittleFS.end()/begin()` as a reboot, format the
filesystem, or reset the board automatically. Use a dedicated test board and
LittleFS with no production data. The test stops on any unexpected queue data.

1. Build only: `pio run -e esp8266-queue-fs-test`.
2. When hardware testing is authorized, install this test firmware on the
   dedicated board and open the serial monitor at 115200 baud.
3. Send `t`. It creates three records, closes the segment with its footer,
   persists a phase marker and leaves the segment in LittleFS.
4. When `TEST PRONTO PARA REBOOT FÍSICO` appears, send `r`, then physically
   press RESET. On the next boot, normal test setup mounts LittleFS and calls
   `recoverQueue()`. It checks segment identity, footer, record contents and
   sequence range, then removes the segment and confirms the queue is empty.
5. Send `r` and physically press RESET again. Boot recovery must find an empty
   queue; it explicitly checks both `/q-seq-a.dat` and `/q-seq-b.dat` high-water
   marks, writes and closes a new record, and checks its segment and record
   sequences are greater than the first run's sequences. It removes this final
   test segment and reports `RESULTADO: PASS`.

Do not send `t` again while a phase marker exists. If a reboot occurs before
the serial confirmation, the same phase remains pending and can be physically
rebooted again after checking the serial output. The default `esp8266`
environment does not enable this test mode. No upload is performed by the build
command above.
